\pard\sb100\sa200\f0\fs36\b Offload\par

\pard\sa200\fs22\b0
Copies the photos and videos you pick from your iPhone to this Mac, organized in Year/Month folders.\par
Keeps the camera's original filenames; Live Photo pairs (photo + .mov) travel together.\par
Nothing is ever deleted from your phone.\par

\pard\sb100\sa200\fs26\b Getting started\par

\pard\sa200\fs22\b0
1. Drag Offload.app to your Applications folder.\par
2. Launch it, pick a folder, choose photos, export. Files land inside an "Offload" subfolder of the folder you picked.\par

\pard\sb100\sa200\fs26\b If macOS blocks the first launch\par

\pard\sa200\fs22\b0
The beta is not notarized, so Gatekeeper may refuse it. Right-click Offload.app, choose Open, then Open again in the dialog.\par
If it still refuses, run this once in Terminal (point it at wherever the app is):\par

\pard\li1440\sa200\f1\fs20
xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine /path/to/Offload.app\par

\pard\sb100\sa200\fs26\b Exporting from your iPhone\par

\pard\sa200\fs22\b0
Plug the phone in and keep it unlocked; approve the trust prompt if one appears. Downloads run one file at a time; leave the app open until the summary screen.\par

\pard\sb100\sa200\fs26\b Beta note\par

\pard\sa200\fs22\b0
Double-clicking the app currently starts with a built-in demo device. To transfer from your real iPhone today, run this instead:\par

\pard\li1440\sa200\f1\fs20
OFFLOAD_DEVICE=real /Applications/Offload.app/Contents/MacOS/Offload\par
